      "question": {
        ":question/id": "7b57bf47-9ce3-51ce-bf7f-debcfe9d7581",
        ":question/problem": "Find ${f}^{′}(x)$ if $f(x)=3\\sqrt{x}+tan⁡x.$\n\n${f}^{′}(x)=$\n{{field-1}}",
        ":question/worked-solution": "We know that $\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(tan⁡x)={sec}^{2}⁡x.$ Applying these formulas, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(3\\sqrt{x}+tan⁡x) \\\\  & =3\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\sqrt{x})+1\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(tan⁡x) \\\\  & =3(\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{x}})+1({sec}^{2}⁡x) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\frac{3}{2}}{\\sqrt{x}}+{sec}^{2}⁡x.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
        ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
        ":question/answer-fields": [
          {
