        ":question/problem": "Find the derivative of $y=\\sqrt{x}+6tan⁡x.$",
        ":question/worked-solution": "We know that $\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(tan⁡x)={sec}^{2}⁡x.$ Applying this formula, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\sqrt{x}+6tan⁡x) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{x}}+6{sec}^{2}⁡x \\\\  & =\\frac{1+12\\sqrt{x}{sec}^{2}⁡x}{2\\sqrt{x}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
