        ":question/problem": "Find the slope of $y=3tan⁡x+6sin⁡x$ at $x=0.$\n\n${y}^{′}(0)=$\n{{field-1}}",
        ":question/worked-solution": "We know that $\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(tan⁡x)={sec}^{2}⁡x$ and $\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(sin⁡x)=cos⁡x.$ Applying these formulas, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(3tan⁡x+6sin⁡x) \\\\  & =3{sec}^{2}⁡x+6cos⁡x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEvaluating at $x=0,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′}(0) & =3{sec}^{2}⁡(0)+6cos⁡(0) \\\\  & =3+6(1) \\\\  & =9.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the slope is $9.$",
